        <h1>LeetCode 3727: Maximum Alternating Sum of Squares (C++)</h1>
        <div class="problem-description">
            <p><strong>Problem:</strong>
                You are given an integer array nums. You may rearrange the elements in any order. The
                alternating score of an array arr is defined as: score = arr[0]^2 - arr[1]^2 + arr[2]^2 -
                arr[3]^2 + ... Return an integer denoting the maximum possible alternating score of nums
                after rearranging its elements.
            </p>
            <p><strong>Example:</strong>
                Input: nums = [1,2,3]<br>
                Output: 12<br>
                Explanation: A possible rearrangement for nums is [2,1,3], which gives the maximum
                alternating score among all possible rearrangements: 2^2 - 1^2 + 3^2 = 4 - 1 + 9 = 12.
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="code-container">
            <button class="copy-button" onclick="copyCode(this)">Copy Code</button>
            <pre><code class="language-cpp">class Solution {
public:
    long long maxAlternatingSum(vector&lt;int&gt;&amp; nums) {
        for (auto &amp;num : nums) {
            if (num &lt; 0) {
                num = -num;
            }
        }

        sort(nums.begin(), nums.end());

        int n = nums.size();
        int left = 0, right = n - 1;
        long long ans = 0;

        while (left &lt; right) {
            ans += 1LL * nums[right] * nums[right]
                 - 1LL * nums[left] * nums[left];
            left++;
            right--;
        }

        if (left == right) {
            ans += 1LL * nums[left] * nums[left];
        }

        return ans;
    }
};</code></pre>
